# Global rules

- Follow root `AGENTS.md` as the entry point for every task.
- Use documentation-first development: read only the docs relevant to the task (see selective strategy in `AGENTS.md`).
- Locate code via `docs/PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md`; avoid unnecessary full-repository scans.
- Preserve existing architecture (Flutter Provider Clean Architecture; Express use cases; Neon + Prisma; Firebase Auth only for identity).
- Verify assumptions in source before implementing; never invent APIs, tables, or product rules.
- Consider cross-layer impacts (Flutter ↔ API ↔ DB ↔ notifications) before changing contracts.
- Update affected `docs/*` in the **same task** when architecture, schema, APIs, business rules, or structure change.
- Run relevant tests after implementation.
- Product authority: `docs/PRODUCT_SCENARIOS.md`. Conflicts are compliance issues until the product owner updates that doc.
- Details live in `docs/`; keep this rule concise.
